WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.033
"What?" The sheriff's cook was stunned by Little John's invitation.

2
00:00:09.034 --> 00:00:12.985
"You're asking me to . . . join Robin Hood's band?

3
00:00:12.986 --> 00:00:15.155
Are you one of his men?"

4
00:00:15.156 --> 00:00:20.467
Little John nodded. "My real name is Little John."

5
00:00:20.468 --> 00:00:23.484
"Little John!" exclaimed the cook.

6
00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:25.899
"I've heard so much about you!

7
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.829
But I never thought I'd meet you.

8
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.945
And you live right here at the sheriff's house!"

9
00:00:31.946 --> 00:00:34.580
"That's right," said Little John.

10
00:00:34.581 --> 00:00:38.446
"But it's time for me to return to my home in Sherwood Forest.

11
00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:41.908
Will you join me—and Robin Hood's band of men?"

12
00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:48.117
"Of course!" The cook was still staring at Little John in amazement.

13
00:00:48.118 --> 00:00:51.869
"I'd be glad to join Robin's band."

14
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.933
Little John grinned.

15
00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:58.854
"Good. Let's take some of the sheriff's silver dishes," he said.

16
00:00:58.855 --> 00:01:02.694
"They'll make a fine gift for Robin."

17
00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.678
"Oh, yes," agreed the cook.

18
00:01:05.679 --> 00:01:09.399
"The sheriff has more silver than he can use."

19
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:16.363
The two men looked around the room for silver, filling a sack with silver bowls, plates, and cups.

20
00:01:16.364 --> 00:01:22.211
Then they set off for Sherwood Forest.

21
00:01:22.212 --> 00:01:25.993
At last they came to a large oak tree.

22
00:01:25.994 --> 00:01:30.801
Robin and a large group of men were lying in the shade on the grass.

23
00:01:30.802 --> 00:01:36.017
"It's Little John!" cried one. All the men jumped to their feet.

24
00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:39.516
"Welcome back, Little John!" said Robin.

25
00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:42.462
"It's been a long time since we've seen you.

26
00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:44.298
How was life with the sheriff?

27
00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:49.240
We heard you were one of his servants."

28
00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:53.482
"The sheriff treated me very well," replied Little John.

29
00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:58.244
"But I knew my real home was here in Sherwood Forest."

30
00:01:58.245 --> 00:02:03.060
The men cheered. "Hooray for Little John!"

31
00:02:03.061 --> 00:02:07.483
"I've brought my new friend, the sheriff's cook," said Little John.

32
00:02:07.484 --> 00:02:12.554
"And we've brought a gift—some of the sheriff's silver."

33
00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:16.628
Little John opened the sack and dumped the dishes on the ground.

34
00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:20.825
Everyone roared with laughter except Robin Hood.

35
00:02:20.826 --> 00:02:24.871
"I'm glad you're back," said Robin with a frown.

36
00:02:24.872 --> 00:02:27.616
"And I'm very happy that you brought a cook.

37
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:32.132
But I don't like that you stole the sheriff's silver.

38
00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:36.908
He tried to fool me once and lost three hundred pounds.

39
00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:41.274
But he hasn't done anything wrong now."

40
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:47.008
Little John shrugged. "Perhaps he'll be glad we have it," he said.

41
00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:49.929
"I have a thought—I'll go fetch him."

42
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:55.891
With that, Little John dashed off through the forest to find the sheriff.

43
00:02:55.892 --> 00:02:59.632
The sheriff was still hunting with his friends.

44
00:02:59.633 --> 00:03:04.899
When Little John finally spotted him, he kneeled and removed his cap.

45
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.746
"Greetings, master."

46
00:03:07.747 --> 00:03:10.970
"Reynold Greenleaf!" cried the sheriff.

47
00:03:10.971 --> 00:03:13.696
"What are you doing here in the woods?"

48
00:03:13.697 --> 00:03:20.067
"I've just seen the most amazing sight near an oak tree, master!" Little John said.

49
00:03:20.068 --> 00:03:25.854
"A huge green deer surrounded by many other green deer!"

50
00:03:25.855 --> 00:03:32.049
The sheriff stared at him. "That's quite a tale. Were you dreaming?"

51
00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.712
"No, I was wide awake," said Little John.

52
00:03:35.713 --> 00:03:39.099
"Come with me and see for yourself."

53
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:44.061
The sheriff was unsure of this tale, but he was also curious.

54
00:03:44.062 --> 00:03:47.973
So he let Little John lead him away from his friends.

55
00:03:47.974 --> 00:03:52.402
At last they drew close to the large oak tree.

56
00:03:52.403 --> 00:03:57.105
"I saw the herd somewhere around here," said Little John.

57
00:03:57.106 --> 00:04:03.037
The sheriff looked around—and spotted Robin and his men!

58
00:04:03.038 --> 00:04:05.893
He spun back toward Little John.

59
00:04:05.894 --> 00:04:09.542
"Now I know who you are. You're Little John!

60
00:04:09.543 --> 00:04:12.032
One day you'll pay for tricking me!"

61
00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.903
Robin came over and greeted the sheriff.

62
00:04:14.904 --> 00:04:20.257
"Welcome, Sheriff. Are you here for another feast?"

63
00:04:20.258 --> 00:04:23.124
"Oh no!" said the sheriff.

64
00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:28.860
He remembered the three hundred pounds he'd lost at Robin's last feast.

65
00:04:28.861 --> 00:04:33.189
"I'm not at all interested in feasting with you again!"

66
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.384
Robin shrugged. "There's your cook," he said.

67
00:04:37.385 --> 00:04:40.265
"You can have anything you like to eat."

68
00:04:40.266 --> 00:04:46.081
The sheriff glared at his cook. "I'm not hungry."

69
00:04:46.082 --> 00:04:50.680
"Surely you'll have something to drink?" said Robin.

70
00:04:50.681 --> 00:04:53.956
One of Robin's men handed the sheriff a drink.

71
00:04:53.957 --> 00:04:59.256
The sheriff gasped. "That's my cup!" he shouted.

72
00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:02.680
"Do you like our new silver?" asked Robin.

73
00:05:02.681 --> 00:05:08.015
"We received a sack of it today." He held up the bag.

74
00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:11.788
The sheriff was so angry, he couldn't speak.

75
00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:14.416
He just stared at the ground.

76
00:05:14.417 --> 00:05:17.707
"You tried to trick me before," said Robin.

77
00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:20.847
"Instead I tricked you.

78
00:05:20.848 --> 00:05:24.165
But this time you weren't doing any harm.

79
00:05:24.166 --> 00:05:27.607
So leave the forest and take your silver with you."

80
00:05:27.608 --> 00:05:30.076
Robin handed him the bag.

81
00:05:30.077 --> 00:05:33.697
The sheriff slowly reached for it.

82
00:05:33.698 --> 00:05:39.588
When he met his hunting friends later, they were full of questions.

83
00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:41.380
"Where did you go?"

84
00:05:41.381 --> 00:05:43.298
"What's in the bag?"

85
00:05:43.299 --> 00:05:45.425
"Where's Reynold Greenleaf?"

86
00:05:45.426 --> 00:05:51.085
The sheriff still felt dazed, confused thoughts tumbling inside his head.

87
00:05:51.086 --> 00:05:55.623
"Never mind. Forget about Reynold Greenleaf!" said the sheriff.

88
00:05:55.624 --> 00:05:59.468
"Let's go home."

